# --- Rust / Cargo ---
/target/
**/target/
# Isolated Cargo home used because the user-level registry mirror is unreachable here.
/.cargo-home/
Cargo.lock.bak

# --- Node / frontend ---
node_modules/
/site/node_modules/
**/node_modules/
/dist/
/site/dist/
/site/.astro/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Tauri build output ---
/src-tauri/target/
/src-tauri/gen/schemas/
/src-tauri/binaries/*.exe

# --- Veloct runtime artefacts (belong to a managed project, not to this repository) ---
.attachments-cache/
.veloct/logs/
*.log

# --- AgentTeams runtime state is not source ---
/.agent-teams/

# --- this session's captured verification output ---
# The raw evidence for the numbers in PROCESSING.md §1. Safe to read, safe to delete, not source.
/.baseline/

# --- local editor / OS noise ---
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp
*.part

# Scratch commit-message files written while composing a commit.
/commit-msg*.txt

# --- a live credential a human pasted into the working directory ---
# `Git.md` holds a real GitHub personal access token and a repository URL. It is a note to the operator, not
# source, and it was NOT ignored until now: `git add -A` would have written a working token into this
# repository's history, where deleting the file afterwards does not remove it. Nothing in Veloct reads this
# file — credentials live in the OS store by handle (`handoff.md` §12), and the live smoke test reads its
# token from the environment (`VELOCT_LIVE_GITHUB_TOKEN`). Ignore it, and ignore the same class of note by
# shape so the next one is safe without anyone remembering this rule.
/Git.md
/*token*.md
/*secret*.md

# --- temporary experiment left over from diagnosing Cargo registry access ---
/.cargo/
dist-ui/

# The pinned Node RUNTIME is fetched and hash-verified rather than committed: it is 89 MB, and putting it in
# every clone and every diff would buy nothing. The pin is `scripts/node-runtime.toml`, the fetch is
# `scripts/fetch-node.ps1`, and ADR-0005 is satisfied because the launcher resolves it from the sidecar path
# and never from PATH. The pattern above already ignores it; this line says so deliberately rather than by
# accident of the `*.exe` rule.
/src-tauri/binaries/veloct-node-*.exe
*.staged

# --- the one generated binary that IS committed ---
# The sidecar LAUNCHER is 2.66 MB of Rust built from `crates/veloct-sidecar`, and Tauri's `externalBin`
# resolves it by its target-triple name at runtime, so it has to be present at that exact path. It is
# re-included HERE, at the end, because git applies these rules in order and a later rule wins: a negation
# placed beside the `*.exe` rule above would simply be overridden by it.
!src-tauri/binaries/veloct-astro-sidecar-*.exe
